| Model | Where it comes from | Introduced or first used here | Used again here |
|---|---|---|---|
| rhythm-syllables | New in kindergarten (mu-k-read, model_out) | Unit 1: "ta" and "ti-ti" spoken with the patted beat, by ear, with no symbols | Unit 5 (the syllables read from picture notation, mu-g1-read), unit 9 (rhythm and melody patterns with a rest, mu-g2-read); every warm-up echo as review |
| describe-interpret-judge | New in kindergarten (mu-k-respond, model_out) | Unit 1: the class listening routine: listen, show it with the body, say what you hear, say if you like it and why | Unit 5 (a purpose shown and judged, mu-g1-respond), unit 9 (a concept described for a purpose, mu-g2-respond); every listen to a work as review |
| expression-map | New in kindergarten (mu-k-express, model_out) | Unit 2: a picture strip of a song with big and small, fast and slow marks | Unit 6 (one song mapped two ways, mu-g1-express), unit 10 (planned loud, soft, fast, slow, smooth and short parts, mu-g2-express); each concert unit's plan as review |
| listening-log | New in kindergarten (mu-k-choose, model_out) | Unit 2: a picture page per piece heard, with a smile scale and a dictated reason | Unit 6 (a pick for a purpose, mu-g1-choose), unit 10 (an explained pick, mu-g2-choose); every unit adds pages |
| idea-bank | New in kindergarten (mu-k-invent, model_out) | Unit 3: the class bundle of motif cards and sound-only recordings | Unit 7 (reply phrases, mu-g1-invent), unit 11 (improvised patterns, mu-g2-invent); each concert unit draws its piece from it |
| notation-ladder | New in kindergarten (mu-k-document, model_out) | Unit 3: picture symbols (big and small dots, high and low places on the card) | Unit 7 (picture or standard notation, mu-g1-document), unit 11 (an A-B piece combined and sequenced, mu-g2-document) |
| critique-protocol | New in kindergarten (mu-k-revise, model_out) | Unit 4: describe what you hear, ask about a choice, suggest one change | Unit 8 (polishing a reply phrase, mu-g1-revise), unit 12 (the child chooses which advice to use, mu-g2-revise); every critique day as review |
| practice-plan | New in kindergarten (mu-k-perform, model_out) | Unit 4: the practice card: echo it in parts, slow then up to speed, hands only | Unit 8 (a strategy on a hard spot, mu-g1-perform), unit 12 (a chosen strategy and a set checklist, mu-g2-perform) |

All eight go on to grade 3 (mu-g3 rows' model_in).

