275: ## Cross-subject
276: 
277: No music row of grades K to 2 carries a cross_subject lean (data/progressions/arts.csv), so this course waits on no
278: other course and no other course waits on it. STANDARD.md 6's music and math lean (note values as fractions) starts in
279: grade 3 (mu-g3-read, math:3.NF.A.1). The contacts below are practiced, not owned, each with its "if later" line; all
280: are core courses (lesson 32), except the physical education boundary, which is a boundary, not a lean.
281: 
282: ### Mathematics, kindergarten to grade 2 (same year)
283: 
284: | Used here | Contact | If math has not taught it yet |
285: |---|---|---|
286: | Unit 1 (year K): eight beats patted and counted | Kindergarten math counts objects one to one in its unit 1 (days 1 to 18) | The music unit counts beats aloud with the teacher only to four, and the beat strip shows hearts to point at; no counting is scored |
287: | Units 7 and 9 (years 1 and 2): twos and threes | Counting to 3 is kindergarten counting | Meter is felt and shown by a conducting pattern; no number work beyond saying "1, 2" or "1, 2, 3" |
288: 
289: No unit asks for note values as parts of a whole, fractions, measuring or adding beats (lesson 13).
290: 
291: ### English language arts, kindergarten to grade 2 (same year)
292: 
293: Talk about works and the critique practice collaborative conversation (SL.K.1, SL.1.1, SL.2.1): practiced, not
294: owned. If ELA has not yet taught the turn-taking rules, the music unit's critique card shows them in pictures (listen,
295: one at a time, then answer) and the teacher models them on the first critique day.
296: 
297: ### Physical education, grades K to 2 (a boundary)
298: 
299: Physical education grade 1 has a dance-to-the-beat unit (its unit 13) and kindergarten units of moves in place. Here
300: children move only to show a music idea (the beat, a tune's shape, loud and soft) by stepping in place, patting and
301: tracing with the hands; the motor skill is PE's, and choreography is dance's (STANDARD.md 6; the dance K to 2 frame,
302: docs/courses/dance-grades-k-to-2/frame.md, moves to a steady beat and to two- and three-beat music). Music units
303: here hear and name the beat and meter; dancing them is dance's. No lean either way.
304: 
305: ## For the lead
306: 
307: 1. **After-core check weeks.** This frame's checks (year K weeks 19 and 25; years 1 and 2 weeks 17 and 25) stay off
308:    every core check week. Read against the K to 2 rows of docs/courses/CALENDAR.md on 2026-11-25, only grade 2 week 17
309:    shares a week with other after-core courses (visual arts, ELD, physical education); weeks 19 (K), 17 (grade 1)
310:    and 25 (all three grades) held no other check that day. Grade 2 has no week free of every check before week 21 that
311:    fits the year's units. Left for the lead's one calendar pass.
312: 2. **MU:Cr2.1.Kb, a browser check.** The national kindergarten music standards, as recalled from memory, may list a
313:    second Cr2.1 part (organizing ideas with picture symbols or a recording) beside choosing favorite ideas; the id file
314:    has 18 kindergarten ids and folds both actions into MU:Cr2.1.Ka's words line. Unit 3 teaches and checks both
315:    actions either way. Pick: the lead opens the music "at a glance" handout and the full standards page in Claude in
316:    Chrome; if Kb exists, add it to the id file and the words file, to mu-k-document's standard cell and to
317:    STANDARD.md 3.2's count (K 19, band 59), and unit 3 names it.
318: 3. **Connecting wording in two rows** (see Row changes): mu-k-choose and mu-g1-choose ask children to share where they
319:    hear music, or the music heard at home. That reads as MU:Cn11 (daily life) more than MU:Cn10 (how tastes,
320:    knowledge and skills shape choices), and it ties the task to home life with no public option. Units 2 and 6 teach
321:    Cn10 as the standard asks, with the option.
322: 4. **Supplies ceiling (money, for Cory).** Provisional costs: $55 (year K), $20 (year 1), $20 (year 2) a class of 30,
323:    all optional beside a free path. Pick: the same ceiling the visual arts K to 2 frame proposes ($75 a class a year),
324:    with every unit's free path kept.
325: 5. **Stagger key.** As the visual arts frame noted, all five arts are subject `arts` in calendar.csv; the 2026-11-25
326:    brief says each after-core course counts on its own, so the music and visual arts checks in grade 2 week 17 are two
327:    checks for the lead's pass.

