"mu","K","mu-k-perform","MU:Pr5.1.Ka; MU:Pr5.1.Kb; MU:Pr6.1.Ka; MU:Pr6.1.Kb","","mu-g1-perform","","practice-plan","practice; again; feedback; expressive; audience; sing","","Use help from self, teacher and peers to improve a performance, try suggested ways to practice, and perform expressively for an audience such as the class. What changes: first year: a performance is improved with help and given to an audience such as the class. Assessed by a performance check: the teacher marks each child's performance as met, partly or not yet. Teacher note: volume stays low, no child is made to sing alone, and a group or recorded version is always an option."
"mu","K","mu-k-choose","MU:Pr4.1.Ka; MU:Re7.1.Ka; MU:Cn10.1.Ka","","mu-g1-choose","","listening-log","favorite; like; choose; why; song; interest","","Bring a song the child likes (or pick one from the class list), tell the class what is good about it, and tell how what the child likes or knows shaped a choice (a song, or a way to sing it), with a story character's choice as an option marked the same. What changes: first year: what interests a child is shown and said. Assessed by a favorites check: the teacher marks each child's show-and-say as met, partly or not yet."
"mu","K","mu-k-respond","MU:Re7.2.Ka; MU:Re9.1.Ka; MU:Cn11.1.Ka","","mu-g1-respond","","describe-interpret-judge","beat; tune; like; judge; art; school","","Move to the beat or show the tune going up and down while a piece plays, say whether the child likes it, and name a story, picture or game the music goes with. What changes: first year: a music idea is shown and a taste is stated. Assessed by a listen-and-say check: the teacher marks each child's answers as met, partly or not yet."
"mu","1","mu-g1-invent","MU:Cr1.1.1a; MU:Cr1.1.1b","mu-k-invent","mu-g2-invent","idea-bank","idea-bank","reply; phrase; purpose; major; minor; twos and threes","","Make a reply phrase for a purpose such as a greeting or a goodnight, and try ideas that sound happy or sad and that move in twos or threes. What changes: a purpose for each idea and a first try at different tonalities and meters. Assessed by a music-making check: the teacher marks each child's phrases as met, partly or not yet."
"mu","1","mu-g1-document","MU:Cr2.1.1a; MU:Cr2.1.1b","mu-k-document","mu-g2-document","notation-ladder","notation-ladder","choose; reason; notation; recording; picture symbols; express","","Play ideas chosen to express an intent, say why they were chosen, and document them in picture or standard notation or in a recording. What changes: the child gives a reason and documents the idea. Assessed by a kept-ideas check: the teacher marks the reason and the record as met, partly or not yet."
"mu","1","mu-g1-revise","MU:Cr3.1.1a; MU:Cr3.2.1a","mu-k-revise","mu-g2-revise","critique-protocol","critique-protocol","feedback; polish; purpose; meaning; share; change","","Play or sing a short idea for a partner and the teacher, change one thing after their feedback, then share the finished music and say what it is for. What changes: the child polishes with less help and says what the music is for. Assessed by a sharing check: the teacher marks the change and the purpose as met, partly or not yet."
"mu","1","mu-g1-read","MU:Pr4.2.1a; MU:Pr4.2.1b","mu-k-read","mu-g2-read","rhythm-syllables","rhythm-syllables","beat; melody direction; picture notation; rhythm; culture; pattern","","Show the beat and which way a tune moves in music from many cultures, and read and perform short rhythm patterns in picture or standard notation. Beat counts and picture symbols only, no note values. What changes: reading begins with simple rhythm patterns from picture symbols. Assessed by a read-and-play task scored on a three-line guide. Teacher note: music from a culture is chosen from that community's own published teaching or a named practitioner. A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."
"mu","1","mu-g1-express","MU:Pr4.3.1a; MU:Re8.1.1a","mu-k-express","mu-g2-express","expression-map","expression-map","loudness; speed; express; creator; performer; show","","Sing one song in two ways (loud and soft, fast and slow) and tell which fits what the song means, then name the choice a recorded performer made. What changes: the child names how loudness and speed carry what a creator means, where kindergarten only noticed them. Assessed by a listen-and-show check scored on a three-line guide."
"mu","1","mu-g1-perform","MU:Pr5.1.1a; MU:Pr5.1.1b; MU:Pr6.1.1a; MU:Pr6.1.1b","mu-k-perform","mu-g2-perform","practice-plan","practice-plan","rehearse; strategy; expressive; purpose; audience; feedback","","Use feedback from self, teacher and peers to improve a performance, try a suggested rehearsal strategy on a hard spot, and perform expressively in a way that fits both the audience and the purpose. What changes: less help, and a performance fitted to an audience and a purpose. Assessed by a performance check: the teacher marks each child's performance as met, partly or not yet."
