"mu","2","mu-g2-document","MU:Cr2.1.2a; MU:Cr2.1.2b","mu-g1-document","mu-g3-document","notation-ladder","notation-ladder","combine; sequence; document; notation; recording; order","","Show and explain why patterns were chosen, then document, combine and sequence ideas in picture or standard notation or a recording. What changes: ideas are combined and put in order, not only kept one by one. Assessed by a documented short piece scored on a three-line guide."
"mu","2","mu-g2-revise","MU:Cr3.1.2a; MU:Cr3.2.2a","mu-g1-revise","mu-g3-revise","critique-protocol","critique-protocol","feedback; revise; sense; mean; for; share","","Play a short piece for self, partner and teacher feedback, choose which advice to use and revise, then share the finished music and tell what it means and what it is for. What changes: the child decides which feedback to use. Assessed by a revised piece and a one-line note on the change, scored on a three-line guide."
