"mu","2","mu-g2-perform","MU:Pr5.1.2a; MU:Pr5.1.2b; MU:Pr6.1.2a; MU:Pr6.1.2b","mu-g1-perform","mu-g3-perform","practice-plan","practice-plan","criteria; accurate; expressive; effective; strategy; rehearse","","Score a class performance with a short checklist, practice one hard spot with a named strategy such as slow, then up to speed, and perform for a purpose such as a morning song. What changes: the child chooses the strategy and judges with set criteria. Assessed by a performance scored on a three-line guide (accurate, expressive, fits the purpose)."
"mu","2","mu-g2-choose","MU:Pr4.1.2a; MU:Re7.1.2a; MU:Cn10.1.2a","mu-g1-choose","mu-g3-choose","listening-log","listening-log","interest; purpose; explain; choose; knowledge; varied","","Choose music for a class purpose from a listening menu and explain the pick, and tell how something the child likes or has done shapes the choice. What changes: the child explains a choice in words, where grade 1 showed and discussed it. Assessed by a short spoken or written reason scored on a three-line guide."
