docs/reviews\units-read-english-language-arts-grade-10-2026-11-24.md:11:The seven units form a sound year: routines open on Frankenstein, each later unit names what it keeps from the one before, and the handoffs into grade 11 (the perceive family, evidence, seminar and syntax rows) are all met. The most serious finding is unit 5's field 4, which put W.9-10.9a (literature) on the rhetoric day 108 and W.9-10.9b (nonfiction) on the novel day 110. That is the reverse of days.csv and field 5, so a writer could build the wrong evidence day. Unit 5 had also swapped the frame's compelling question for Pope's poem title. The rest is minor drift: unit 6's word-list week label, unit 2's unnamed seminars, and source and supply lines the old cap had pushed out.
# source: https://www.nationalartsstandards.org/sites/default/files/2021-11/Dance%20at%20a%20Glance.pdf
# source: https://www.nationalartsstandards.org/sites/default/files/2021-11/Media%20Arts%20at%20a%20Glance.pdf
# source: https://nationalartsstandards.org/sites/default/files/2021-11/Music%20at%20a%20Glance.pdf
# source: https://nationalartsstandards.org/sites/default/files/2021-11/Theatre%20at%20a%20Glance.pdf
# source: https://www.nationalartsstandards.org/sites/default/files/2021-11/Visual%20Arts%20at%20a%20Glance%20rev.pdf
# version: National Core Arts Standards (NCCAS 2014; "at a glance" handouts dated 2021-11 on nationalartsstandards.org)
# fetched: 2026-10-27
# level: one lettered performance-standard statement, DIS:<Process><Anchor>.<Std>.<Grade><letter>; grades PK, K, 1-8, I/II/III = HS Proficient/Accomplished/Advanced
# anchors: 1-3 Creating (Cr1 generate/conceptualize, Cr2 organize/develop, Cr3 refine/complete)
# anchors: 4-6 Performing (DA, MU, TH) / Presenting (VA) / Producing (MA) (Pr4 select/analyze/interpret, Pr5 develop/refine, Pr6 convey meaning)
# anchors: 7-9 Responding (Re7 perceive/analyze, Re8 interpret intent/meaning, Re9 apply criteria to evaluate)
# anchors: 10-11 Connecting (Cn10 synthesize/relate knowledge and experience, Cn11 relate to societal, cultural, historical context)
# note: performance standards per grade: DA 11, MA 11, MU 15, TH 12 (Cn11.1 and Cn11.2), VA 15 (Cr1.1, Cr1.2, Cr2.1, Cr2.2, Cr2.3, Re7.1, Re7.2 ...). Grade cells: DA 143, MA 143, MU 150, TH 156, VA 195 (all present).
# note: MUSIC = the PK-8 general music strand plus, since 2026-11-21, the high school Composition and Theory strand (63 ids, MU:...C.Ia to .C.IIIb, docs/courses/arts/STANDARD.md 3.3). The other HS music strands (Traditional and Emerging Ensembles, Harmonizing Instruments, Technology) are NOT included.
# note: letters were derived by parsing the handouts' cell layout (positions of the a./b./c. markers), not copied from a published list; NCCAS publishes no letter-level total. Cross-check: b and c item counts equal the raw PDF text counts for DA, MA, TH; for MU the raw text undercounts (spot-checked cells MU:Cr3.1.6-8 by hand). VA prints every code with its letter (all "a").
# note: Media Arts prints single-statement cells with no letter (e.g. MA:Cr1.1.5), so those lines carry no letter; multi-statement MA cells are lettered (MA:Cr3.1.5a, MA:Cr3.1.5b).
